dialect protocol
protocol stdio.obj.diff
version 1
schema stdio.obj.diff
start diff

# P2-FG1 fixup wave: REAL binary diff frame, replacing the OLDER `Ok(self.print_diff().into_bytes())`
# text-as-binary shortcut (`../🦀️.rs`'s upgraded `DiffCodec::encode_diff`/`decode_diff`,
# `#region 🔖️TopLevel`) — `obj` was one of 4 stdio standards (alongside stl/step/ifc4) the FG1
# wave's own verify agent found still on that shortcut, despite md/xml/dxf proving the real
# upgrade achievable THIS SAME WAVE for equally-flat/recursive types. `ObjDiff` is hand-rolled
# (§3b tri-state blocker documented at the top of `../🦀️.rs` —
# `ObjVertexDiff::w`/`ObjTexCoordDiff::w`/`ObjDiff::mtllib` are all `Option<Option<T>>`, which
# `#[derive(dsl::DslDiff)]`'s `classify_field` cannot express), so this still does NOT route
# through the framework-generic `.spk` document container the way a genuinely `DslDiff`-derived
# diff type would.
#
# `format u8` (`store::pack_rt::OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `flags_lo u8` + `flags_hi u8` (a
# 10-bit presence mask across TWO bytes — `ObjDiff` has TEN independently optional top-level
# fields, one more than a single `flags u8` byte can hold, unlike dxf's four-field `DxfDiff`:
# flags_lo bit0=vertices bit1=texcoords bit2=normals bit3=faces bit4=groups bit5=objects
# bit6=mtllib bit7=usemtl; flags_hi bit0=smoothing_groups bit1=unknown_statements) are the three
# REAL fixed header fields; each PRESENT field's own payload follows as one opaque trailing
# `bytes` chain — genuinely field-by-field structured, varint/fixed-8-byte-f64 binary at the Rust
# layer (`enc_vertices_diff_bin`/`enc_texcoords_diff_bin`/`enc_normals_diff_bin`/
# `enc_faces_diff_bin`/`enc_groups_diff_bin`/`enc_objects_diff_bin`/`write_option_bin`/
# `write_vec_bin` in `../🦀️.rs`'s `#region 🔖️CollectionBinaryCodecs`), not re-modeled
# field-by-field HERE because `Prim::Ref` unconditionally errors on this kind of
# collection-of-records structure during `walk_protocol` (`protocol-prim-ref-recursion` /
# `protocol-array-of-records`, the recipe's own consolidated gap table — every pilot with a
# collection-triple diff independently hit and worked around the same wall, same as dxf's own
# `DxfDiff` protocol file's identical framing). `ObjDiff`'s own value/struct layer (vertex,
# texcoord, normal, face, group, object, usemtl/smoothing/unknown ranges) is genuinely FLAT — no
# further nested `Vec<Record>` inside those — so unlike md's recursive block tree, nothing at the
# scalar layer needs opacity; only the collection-triple SHAPE itself does.
framing record
header fixed 3
field format u8
field flags_lo u8
field flags_hi u8
chain payload bytes
